WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.304
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:09.234
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:14.740
Unit seventeen: Would like / Want. Today you will ask for things and make polite offers.

4
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.530
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.607
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.451
Would like.

7
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.135
Would like means a polite way to say you want something.

8
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.227
I would like some tea.

9
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:32.248
Your turn. Say: Would like.

10
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.939
Would like.

11
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:37.348
Want.

12
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.593
Want means to wish to have or do something.

13
00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:42.359
I want a drink.

14
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.324
Your turn. Say: Want.

15
00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.168
Want.

16
00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:50.883
Polite.

17
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:53.778
Polite means showing good manners.

18
00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:55.698
She is very polite.

19
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:58.425
Your turn. Say: Polite.

20
00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.128
Polite.

21
00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:03.954
Request.

22
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.878
Request means a polite way of asking for something.

23
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:09.960
I made a request.

24
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.585
Your turn. Say: Request.

25
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:17.446
Request.

26
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:18.964
Wish.

27
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.938
Wish means to hope for something.

28
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.690
I wish you luck.

29
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.425
Your turn. Say: Wish.

30
00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.210
Wish.

31
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:31.893
I'd like.

32
00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:35.312
I'd like means the short form of I would like.

33
00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:37.440
I'd like a glass of water.

34
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.319
Your turn. Say: I'd like.

35
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.086
I'd like.

36
00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:45.700
Offer.

37
00:01:46.717 --> 00:01:49.355
Offer means something that you say you will give or do.

38
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.265
Thank you for your offer.

39
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.142
Your turn. Say: Offer.

40
00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.059
Offer.

41
00:01:58.817 --> 00:01:59.736
Preference.

42
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.051
Preference means a choice you like better.

43
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:05.255
My preference is tea.

44
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.735
Your turn. Say: Preference.

45
00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.624
Preference.

46
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.956
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.817 --> 00:02:21.746
Visal, you are in a restaurant. How do you ask politely for water?

48
00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:30.799
I would like a glass of water, please. Would like is more polite than want. In shops and restaurants we use I'd like or Could I have.

49
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:33.244
How do we make an offer?

50
00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:44.043
Would you like some tea? It is a polite offer. We can answer Yes, please or No, thank you. We do not say Yes, I would, because it sounds cold.

51
00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.743
What comes after would like?

52
00:02:47.850 --> 00:03:02.210
A noun or to + base verb: I would like a coffee. I would like to book a table. After want we use the same patterns, but want sounds direct. Use polite words at work and with strangers.

53
00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.762
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.617 --> 00:03:07.976
Grammar focus: Would like and want.

55
00:03:08.276 --> 00:03:09.428
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.117 --> 00:03:12.290
I would like a glass of water, please.

57
00:03:13.183 --> 00:03:14.579
Would you like some tea?

58
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:17.088
I would like to book a table.

59
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:26.270
Would like is more polite than want. Use it for requests and offers: I'd like…, Would you like…? After it, use a noun or to + base verb.

60
00:03:27.017 --> 00:03:30.923
Be careful! Don't say: I want to booking a table.

61
00:03:32.867 --> 00:03:34.831
Say: I would like to book a table.

62
00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:37.026
Use the base verb after to.

63
00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:40.520
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:42.718
Ordering Politely.

65
00:03:43.018 --> 00:03:46.041
Good evening. I would like a table for two, please.

66
00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:50.197
Would you like something to drink? I'd like some tea.

67
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.815
My friend wants noodles, but I prefer rice.

68
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.183
That is my preference, because I love soup.

69
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.723
A polite request makes everyone happy.

70
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:06.230
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:07.083 --> 00:04:08.955
I blank a glass of water, please.

72
00:04:09.255 --> 00:04:12.862
A, would like. B, like would. C, am like.

73
00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.179
The answer is A: would like.

74
00:04:19.317 --> 00:04:20.980
blank you like some coffee?

75
00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.225
A, Do. B, Would. C, Are.

76
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.511
The answer is B: Would.

77
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.464
Which sounds more polite?

78
00:04:32.764 --> 00:04:37.892
A, I want a table.. B, I'd like a table, please.. C, Give me a table..

79
00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:44.362
The answer is B: I'd like a table, please..

80
00:04:45.517 --> 00:04:47.238
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:47.538 --> 00:04:52.120
A, I would like to booking.. B, I would like to book.. C, I would like book..

82
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:58.038
The answer is B: I would like to book..

83
00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:02.286
According to the reading, what does the friend prefer?

84
00:05:02.586 --> 00:05:05.845
A, noodles. B, tea. C, soup.

85
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.330
The answer is A: noodles.

86
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:15.813
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.393
Write a polite request using 'would like' at a restaurant.

88
00:05:28.183 --> 00:05:29.672
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:29.972 --> 00:05:40.234
Good evening. I would like a table for two, please. We would like to see the menu, and I'd like some water. I use would like to be polite when I speak to the waiter.

90
00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.185
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:46.873
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and would like and want.

92
00:05:47.173 --> 00:05:51.103
Today's value is politeness. Say please and thank you.

93
00:05:51.403 --> 00:05:54.113
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:54.413 --> 00:05:57.112
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

